!------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Users should ONLY USE user_nl_dart to change namelist variables
! for namelist variables in DART input.nml.
! Users should add ALL user specific namelist changes below using the
! following syntax:
!
! &namelist
! namelist_var = new_namelist_value
! /
!
! This file applies to ALL active DA components.
!
! To override settings for a specific component only, create a file
! named user_nl_dart_{comp} in $CASEROOT, e.g.:
!   user_nl_dart_atm   (atmosphere)
!   user_nl_dart_ocn   (ocean)
!   user_nl_dart_lnd   (land)
!   user_nl_dart_ice   (sea-ice)
!
! Settings in user_nl_dart_{comp} take precedence over this file for
! that component. Both files may be used together.
!
! Note that some namelist variables MAY NOT be changed in user_nl_dart -
! they are defined in a $CASEROOT xml file and must be changed with
! xmlchange.
!
!------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Inflation
!
! With inf_initial_from_restart / inf_sd_initial_from_restart = .true.,
! inflation is read from the restart written by the previous assimilation
! cycle.  On the FIRST cycle of a new case there is no such file yet, so
! assimilate.py turns the from_restart flags off for that cycle only and
! filter starts from inf_initial / inf_sd_initial below.  Set them to the
! values you want inflation to begin at; from the second cycle onward they
! are ignored, because inflation comes from the restart file.
!
! inf_sd_initial must be greater than zero for inflation to adapt.  With
! inf_sd_initial = 0.0 (the template default) inflation stays fixed at
! inf_initial for the WHOLE run, not just the first cycle: the zero is
! written into the inflation restart and read back every cycle after.
! 0.6 is a common starting value.  dart_log.out reports 'time-constant'
! instead of 'time-adaptive' inflation when this happens.
!
!------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Ensemble perturbation (tutorial / cold-start cases)
!
! Set perturb_from_single_instance = .true. below for a multi-instance case
! where every instance starts from an identical restart (e.g. the
! tutorial). assimilate.py then restricts it to cycle 0 only: cycle 0
! perturbs instance 1's restart into the full ensemble; every cycle after
! is forced back to .false. regardless of this setting, because by then the
! instances have diverged through assimilation and the real, by-then-
! diverged per-instance restarts must be used instead.
!
! If you leave this .false. (the default), nothing is forced on at any
! cycle.
!
! perturbation_amplitude controls how large the cycle-0 perturbation
! is.  It is ignored once perturb_from_single_instance is .false.
!
! WARNING: if you resubmit a job mid-experiment with this still set to
! .true., CIME's cycle counter restarts at 0 for the new job segment, and
! cycle 0 will perturb again, discarding the ensemble spread already built
! up.  Set it back to .false. before resubmitting an in-progress
! multi-cycle experiment.
!
!------------------------------------------------------------------------

